WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.880
"The Suicide Squad" is the first DC film from&nbsp;
James Gunn, and it's overflowing with darkly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.360
disturbed heroes, visually stunning sequences,&nbsp;
and sizzling dialogue. Here are some lines in "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.720
Suicide Squad" that mean more than you might&nbsp;
have realized the first time you heard them.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.880
When Amanda Waller introduces&nbsp;
Robert DuBois, aka Bloodsport,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:20.400
these are the bona fides that she&nbsp;
chooses to highlight on his resume:
 &nbsp;

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.160
"He's in prison for putting Superman&nbsp;
in the ICU with a kryptonite bullet."
 &nbsp;

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:27.760
This line has three purposes. First and&nbsp;
foremost, it establishes that although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.280
DuBois doesn't have any superpowers, he&nbsp;
possesses a skillset formidable enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:35.600
to take down anyone, even arguably the&nbsp;
most powerful hero in all of comic-dom.&nbsp;

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.280
Secondly, it tells us this threat is&nbsp;
rooted in not only stellar marksmanship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:43.200
but also his high-tech suit and weaponry that&nbsp;
manifests itself, ensuring that he always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.680
has the right weapon for any given situation.
The third purpose is to establish the stakes for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:52.080
the film's biggest showdown. Near the end of the&nbsp;
film, as Jotunheim is collapsing and Peacemaker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:56.880
is moments away from executing Ratcatcher II,&nbsp;
DuBois comically surfs from floor to floor, each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:01.600
collapsing beneath him as he tries to stay steady&nbsp;
— depositing him right into the confrontation.&nbsp;

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.920
Realizing the situation, Peacemaker turns his gun&nbsp;
on Bloodsport — and if you don't immediately know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:09.920
who's going to win that shootout, you weren't&nbsp;
listening very closely to Waller's introduction.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:15.280
"Each member was chosen for his or her&nbsp;
own completely unique set of abilities."
 &nbsp;

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:18.800
Another line from Waller, and this time the&nbsp;
director of A.R.G.U.S. seems to be tipping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.560
off not only her own status as puppet&nbsp;
master, but also a game plan that stacks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:27.520
the deck against the majority of Task Force X.
Most literally, the line foreshadows a comical,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.720
bloody opening that kills off several&nbsp;
characters. Why would Waller choose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.960
Blackguard, Captain Boomerang, TDK,&nbsp;
Javelin, Mongal, and Savant to storm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:39.520
a beach filled with armed-to-the-teeth soldiers?
None of these "chosen" fighters are bulletproof,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:42.640
or have powers that could unarm the&nbsp;
soldiers with the wave of a hand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:46.720
They are little more than bait on a hook, selected&nbsp;
to make a whole bunch of noise and not much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:51.200
else. It's also very hard to believe that someone&nbsp;
as thorough as Waller would select Weasel and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:56.000
not know perfectly well that he couldn't swim.
It's just a distraction, of course — which is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.000
interesting, not only because Waller clearly&nbsp;
wanted Bloodsport, Peacemaker, King Shark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.480
Ratcatcher II, and Polka-Dot Man to be her "A"&nbsp;
team, but also because by placing Colonel Rick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:08.720
Flag and Harley Quinn on her "B" team, was she&nbsp;
hoping for them to also be mowed down in a hail&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:13.360
of gunfire upon reaching the shores of Corto&nbsp;
Maltese? Waller is surprised to learn that Flag&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:17.680
survived the slaughter, and doesn't seem to have&nbsp;
plans for Harley Quinn beyond the beach, either.&nbsp;

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:20.560
So in essence, that line is Waller&nbsp;
saying: "Everybody whose unique set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:24.560
of abilities we need will be on the 'A' team.&nbsp;
Everybody chosen for useless powers that will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.560
distract the enemy are on the 'B' team, and&nbsp;
they'll make a big ruckus before they die."&nbsp;

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.560
Now, if you were to ask Harley Quinn after the&nbsp;
events of the movie, she'd tell you that Javelin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:36.720
did serve a purpose — and that purpose was to give&nbsp;
her the weapon she would eventually need to stop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:39.280
Starro and save the day.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.440
"We're all gonna die." 
 
"I hope so."
 &nbsp;

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:45.680
This early moment from Abner Krill — whose&nbsp;
page-bound predecessor James Gunn endearingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:49.600
describes as "the dumbest DC character&nbsp;
of all time" — reminds us of what Gunn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:54.160
does better than any modern filmmaker: Take&nbsp;
an idea that sounds terrible and delicately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:58.800
transform it into something audiences will love.
By the end of the film, Polka-Dot Man will likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.400
be your favorite "Suicide Squad" member. Also&nbsp;
by the end of the film, he will have come a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:06.640
long way from the self-loathing Debbie Downer&nbsp;
wishing death upon himself and his Squad-mates.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:10.880
Krill has more issues than Sports Illustrated,&nbsp;
to be sure — chief among them a deep hatred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:15.200
for the mother he envisions as every enemy he&nbsp;
hopes to obliterate — but as the film goes on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:18.400
he finds true joy through the&nbsp;
mission and the camaraderie therein.&nbsp;

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:22.320
This particularly feels true with Polka-Dot&nbsp;
Man's moment on the dance floor just before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.000
the team captures the Thinker, when he seems&nbsp;
to let his hair down for the first time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:29.860
Another factor of growth seems to be a&nbsp;
genuine friendship with Ratcatcher II, who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:34.480
is also the most bothered by his eventual fate.
When all is said and done, Polka-Dot Man is as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.640
into his job as any of us in the audience who hope&nbsp;
to live vicariously through these characters. 
 &nbsp;

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:42.560
"I'm a superhero!"

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:46.401
"Starfish is a slang term for butthole.&nbsp;
Think there's any connection?"

00:03:48.451 --> 00:03:49.663
"No."

00:03:49.663 --> 00:03:51.200
Yeah, it's a funny line. Yeah, it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:56.320
very James Gunn, and yeah, it got a big laugh in&nbsp;
the trailer. But it's also a totally fake moment.&nbsp;

00:03:56.320 --> 00:04:00.000
As we learn later in the film, Peacemaker&nbsp;
was the only member of the Suicide Squad who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.560
got the "real" briefing on this&nbsp;
mission. With that knowledge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:05.520
how can this exchange be seen as&nbsp;
anything other than a duplicitous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:09.440
attempt to establish Peacemaker as too&nbsp;
lunkheaded to have an ulterior motive?&nbsp;

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:13.440
He already knows he's really going to Corto&nbsp;
Maltese to destroy files linking the U.S. to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:17.760
Jotunheim and kill any of his teammates who get&nbsp;
in the way; he also likely knows that "Project&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:22.320
Starfish" refers to a giant space starfish that&nbsp;
has been experimented on there for decades.&nbsp;

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:26.720
Of course, this also means Waller is faking her&nbsp;
frustration with his question — she knows quite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:31.920
well that Peacemaker's overzealous note-taking&nbsp;
is a façade, one quite likely devised by her.&nbsp;

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:36.160
In reality, James Gunn told Cena on the set&nbsp;
to play the character like "a bro'd up version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:40.480
of Captain America." By the end of the film,&nbsp;
it's clear that Peacemaker isn't this stupid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:43.520
and also that he's arguably the most&nbsp;
villainous of all these villains.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:46.240
In the DC Extended Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:51.280
there's no such thing as COVID-19. Lucky them;&nbsp;
all they have to fear are brain-sucking starfish,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:55.440
child-murdering weasels, and walking sharks&nbsp;
that might mistake them for a "num-num."&nbsp;

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.880
As all of us are well too aware, "The&nbsp;
Suicide Squad" is among the many,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:03.760
many blockbuster films impacted by the worldwide&nbsp;
pandemic that put much of pop culture on hold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:08.240
(for good reason) beginning in 2020. Much of the&nbsp;
film was edited at the writer-director's home in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:13.280
the latter half of 2020, as coronavirus forced&nbsp;
many people to work remotely. Of course, James&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:18.080
Gunn knows all this — and in his own sly way, he&nbsp;
wants to acknowledge the elephant in the room.&nbsp;

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:21.440
So, on the verge of the climactic battle&nbsp;
in Jotunheim, when the Squad briefs the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:25.440
Thinker on the rules of engagement, Harley&nbsp;
Quinn plays comic relief, telling the mad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:29.520
scientist which actions will get him killed.
 
"If you cough without covering your mouth—" 
 &nbsp;

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:33.120
"Harley! Although, that isn't an open invitation&nbsp;
for you to cough without covering your mouth."
 &nbsp;

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:36.880
So if you plan to see "The Suicide Squad" in&nbsp;
theaters, take it from Harley Quinn and Colonel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:41.280
Flag and be mindful of germ-spreading. Wash&nbsp;
your hands, wear your mask where applicable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:45.360
and try not to cough while Task Force X&nbsp;
are explaining the rules. Because we all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:50.000
know now what happens to the Thinker — and you&nbsp;
definitely do not want to end up like that guy.

